codex
The reference semantics already models `hashlib.md5(...).hexdigest()` as a trusted opaque digest function. I’m using that intended abstraction: the symbolic theorem will prove the implementation returns `noneV` exactly for the empty string and returns `md5hexCodes(CS)` for every nonempty symbolic string, which is stronger and more honest than postulating a one-off equation for the prompt’s example.
