codex
The LLVM backend exposed the semantics’ documented boundary: a nonempty call reaches the opaque `md5hexCodes(...)` oracle, and LLVM exits 113 because that symbol deliberately has no evaluator. That does not affect the Haskell proof. I’m separating the successful concrete empty-branch run from an explicitly expected-failure oracle-boundary probe, so `prove.sh` records both behaviors without misreporting the latter as a successful concrete digest computation.
apply patch
